# # EXP343 arm (carried over from EXP338) 'weedlag': weed-blocked BUILD_PASTURE/BUILD_COOP/PLANT recovery by one-step lag replay.
# # The chassis already DIGs a weed under a PLANT/BUILD target and queues the intended action, but drops the queue as soon
# # as the tape moves the unit away, so a pasture is never built and the cow bought for it stays in the shed all game
# # (live: 2 of 126 games, about -1.5k..-2k each; V48 mirror on such a world loses ~2000 at that seat). After the DIG,
# # replay the intended action next step, then keep that unit one step behind its tape for a bounded number of steps so
# # the placement sequence (PICKUP -> walk -> PLACE) is executed intact. Pattern after salemali7, "Kaggriculture | 2900+"
# # (public notebook, Apache-2.0), reimplemented on the V48 route tables. Other units and the market are untouched.
# # hands are re-hired each day; lag state cannot survive the day boundary
